# Real input packets for the host Explorer run, in order. Read by
# tools/probe_application.cpp through --click-script.
#
# The desktop's RunOnce entry raises two RUNDLL error boxes about a driver this
# installation registers but does not ship. A user would close them, so the
# script does, before it touches the taskbar.
dialog RUNDLL
dialog RUNDLL
wait 1000
shot build/start-menu-2/step-0.ppm
# Press the Start button, the taskbar's only Button child. Its final rectangle
# is 2,576 to 50,598, so the centre of the window is the button itself.
window Button
wait 3000
shot build/start-menu-2/step-1.ppm
wait 3000
shot build/start-menu-2/step-2.ppm
# The click is worth about 95,000 API calls of original SHELL32 walking the
# seeded folder, including the two PifMgr_OpenProperties calls behind flat thunk
# index 5. After that the guest parks in its message loop with no menu. Three
# more minutes change nothing; the last capture records that.
wait 60000
wait 60000
wait 60000
shot build/start-menu-2/step-3.ppm
# From here on the menu would have to be open: Programs, then Accessories,
# then Notepad. It never opens, so those steps are not in the script yet.
